Subject: Assert glibc overflow behavior in the printf fixture
Description: Peios runs Bash's upstream test suite as a build gate on
 glibc, whose snprintf rejects an over-range inline precision. The fixture
 now records the glibc result (status 1, empty variable) instead of another
 libc's output. The overflow case and the following %Q test still run.
Author: Peios maintainers <packaging@peios.org>
Origin: vendor, Linux/glibc test fixture adaptation
Forwarded: no

# glibc snprintf rejects an inline precision exceeding its integer range.
# The host glibc Bash reproduces status 1 and an empty variable for this input.
# Record that Linux/glibc result; do not skip the overflow or following %Q test.
--- a/tests/printf.right
+++ b/tests/printf.right
@@ -388,5 +388,6 @@
 [X]
 VAR=[]
 VAR=[X]
+./printf7.sub: line 88: printf: Value too large for defined data type
+
 XY
-XY
